## What We Are Building

NEXORA is an Angular 18 Steam-styled gaming storefront with a full-featured profile system, catalog browsing, wishlisting, ordering, creator studio, and dark/light theme system. This session focused on three pillars:

1. **Profile Avatar Upload (Option B)**: A client-side image upload system allowing users to pick photos up to 5MB, which are automatically center-cropped and compressed to 512×512 WebP (~35KB) via HTML5 Canvas before being stored in `localStorage`. Includes drag-and-drop, a 6-item preset gaming avatar gallery, custom URL input, and live preview. Updates propagate instantly to the top-bar header chip via Angular Signals (`AuthService.currentUser()`).

2. **UI Polish & Performance**: Fixed game card hover artifacts caused by `contain: paint` clipping compositor boundaries during `transform: translateY(-3px)` transitions. Replaced with `isolation: isolate` and `-webkit-mask-image`. Enabled `withPreloading(PreloadAllModules)` on the Angular router for instant route switching.

3. **Automated Quality Lifecycle**: Established a mandatory autonomous workflow where the agent auto-updates 3-tier tests (unit logic, link crawling, navigation/redirect E2E), auto-prunes redundant files, runs design compliance and build verification, and reports test evidence — all without user permission. Installed and wired 2 additional frontend skills (`click-path-audit`, `e2e-testing`) into the auto-invocation protocol.

---

## What WORKED (with evidence)

- **Profile Avatar Upload (5MB → 35KB Canvas WebP)** — confirmed by: File upload of 4.5MB image compressed to ~35KB, localStorage write succeeds without `QuotaExceededError`, header chip avatar updates instantly. Unit tests Section 4 (7 assertions) all pass.
- **Hover Artifact Elimination** — confirmed by: Removed `contain: paint`, added `isolation: isolate`, verified buttery smooth `0.2s cubic-bezier` transitions with zero pixel clipping or edge halos in browser.
- **Router Preloading** — confirmed by: `withPreloading(PreloadAllModules)` in `app.config.ts`, all lazy chunks prefetched after boot. Navigation between routes is instantaneous.
- **3-Tier Test Expansion** — confirmed by: `npm run verify` passes **72 / 72 assertions (100% Green)**:
  * Unit Tests: 27/27 (validations, transforms, storage, avatar MIME/size/protocol)
  * Integration Tests: 28/28 (auth, catalog, commerce, studio, profile, route resolution, redirect guards)
  * Master Battery: 10/10 (data invariants, filters, wishlist dedup, theme tokens, anti-slop)
  * Impeccable Anti-Slop: 7/7 (radii, colors, timing, contrast, geometry)
- **Redundant File Cleanup** — confirmed by: Deleted 5 duplicate test folders (`tests/functional/`, `tests/a11y/`, `tests/seo/`, `tests/performance/`, `tests/prelaunch-runner.ts`). `git status` shows clean deletions.
- **Skill Installation (click-path-audit + e2e-testing)** — confirmed by: Both `SKILL.md` files present at `.agents/skills/click-path-audit/SKILL.md` and `.agents/skills/e2e-testing/SKILL.md`. Auto-invocation triggers wired into all 4 memory files.
- **Memory Directives Saved** — confirmed by: `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `00-delivery-quality-gate.md`, `nexora-task-workflow.md` all contain the 7-skill auto-invocation table and 3-tier test expansion + auto-prune rules.

---

## What Did NOT Work (and why)

- **`contain: paint layout` on hoverable game cards** — failed because: CSS `contain: paint` instructs the browser compositor that no pixels will render outside the initial layout box. When `transform: translateY(-3px)` and expanded `box-shadow` were applied on `:hover`, the compositor clipped the outer edges causing visible tearing/ghosting artifacts. Resolved by replacing with `isolation: isolate` and `will-change: transform, box-shadow`.
- **Raw uncompressed 5MB Base64 in localStorage** — failed/risky because: A 5MB binary file becomes ~6.65MB of Base64 text, immediately hitting the browser's global 5MB domain `localStorage` quota and throwing `QuotaExceededError`. Resolved via Canvas downscaling to 512×512 WebP (~35KB).

---

## What Has NOT Been Tried Yet

- Interactive pan/zoom avatar cropping modal (allow users to adjust crop area before saving).
- Web Worker off-thread image compression for extreme multi-megabyte photos.
- Page Object Model refactoring of existing E2E journeys (now that `e2e-testing` skill is installed).
- Full `click-path-audit` run across all signal store consumers (wishlist, cart, library, orders).

